{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract vcf chain-annotate [-h] [--vcf-input VCF_INPUT] [--annotations ANNOTATIONS]\n                                     [--keep-intermediates] [-r REGION] [--bed BED] [--force]\n                                     [--force-step STEP] [--to-table]\n                                     [--table-format {tsv,parquet}]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --vcf-input VCF_INPUT\n                        Optional override for VCF input file.\n  --annotations ANNOTATIONS\n                        Comma-separated list of annotations to apply in order (default:\n                        clinvar,revel,phylop,gnomad,vep).\n  --keep-intermediates  Keep intermediate VCFs after success so later runs can reuse them.\n  -r, --region REGION   Only annotate this region (e.g. chr22:1000-2000) or comma-separated\n                        regions.\n  --bed BED             Only annotate regions in this 0-based BED or BED.gz file.\n  --to-table            Also export a variant table and SQLite database.\n  --table-format {tsv,parquet}\n                        Format with --to-table (default: tsv).\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nresuming:\n  Completed steps are recorded in <output>.steps.json and skipped when a rerun's inputs,\n  settings and tools are unchanged.\n\n  --force, --no-resume, --restart\n                        Rerun every step, ignoring the steps an earlier run completed.\n  --force-step, --force-steps STEP\n                        Rerun STEP and the steps that use its outputs (repeatable). Steps: select,\n                        clinvar, revel, phylop, cadd, gerp, gnomad, spliceai, alphamissense,\n                        pharmgkb, vep, trim.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract vcf chain-annotate --vcf-input sample.vcf.gz --annotations clinvar,gnomad --region chr22:19000000-20000000 --threads 4 --to-table\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  chain_annotated.vcf.gz (+ index), chain_annotate.steps.json; with --to-\n  table, chain_annotated_variants.tsv (or .parquet) and .sqlite.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools, tabix; depending on options and inputs, also: bgzip, samtools,\n  vep, vep-rs; minutes on a 30x genome.\n",
